  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Overlap Issues**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s report about overlapping elements: the title \"Ethics\", the text \"ROLE PARA EXPLORAR\", the arrow, and the subtitle \"Constant Transparency.\" I\'m now investigating the bottom badges of the section (lines 66-80) to understand the layout\'s structure, identify the source of the overlap, and determine the most effective approach to resolve it.\n\n\n**Investigating Structure & Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the bottom badges, specifically lines 66-80 of the code. I am dissecting their structure. I can see a three-column layout, but only the first two columns display on smaller screens. I am correlating this now with the apparent overlap issue reported.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Overlap Source**\n\nI\'ve isolated the scroll indicator\'s positioning as the root cause. Its absolute positioning (`absolute bottom-2 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2`) creates a potential overlap with the \"\303\211tica\" badge, particularly on smaller screens where the layout condenses. I\'m focusing now on how the bottom badges are structured relative to the scroll indicator in the original code, as well as the behavior of the `grid` layout.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the user\'s intended relationship between \"ROLE PARA EXPLORAR\" and the \"\303\211tica\" badge. Are they meant to be merged, or simply ordered? I am re-examining the provided instructions, specifically the vertical order requirement, to definitively determine if the text should be *within* the \"\303\211tica\" badge block, or adjacent to it, and how that relates to the overlap issue.\n\n\n**Revising Layout Strategy**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s requirement to merge the \"ROLE PARA EXPLORAR\" elements with \"\303\211tica\", the arrow, and \"Transpar\303\252ncia constante\" into a combined, vertically-ordered flow. I am interpreting that the third column\'s structure will need modification. I am also reviewing the spacing instructions: a minimum of 12px between the title and its helper text, 16px between the helper text, arrow, and subtitle. And centralizing the new merged element!\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Centering Intent**\n\nI am now reconsidering the implications of the centering directive. Initially, I thought it applied to the scroll indicator if I integrate it. However, the user\'s \"Centralizar corretamente o conjunto\" likely refers to the merged block encompassing \"\303\211tica\" and the new content. I am now experimenting with centering this combined third column within the grid layout, while keeping the other elements aligned as specified, as it is the \"conjunto\" the user is referring to.\n\n\n**Structuring New Section**\n\nI am now structuring the new section based on user requirements. My plan is to remove \"ROLE PARA EXPLORAR\" from the absolutely positioned container and place it within the \"\303\211tica\" block, which is the third column. Then, I will vertically order the elements: \"\303\211tica,\" \"ROLE PARA EXPLORAR,\" the arrow, and \"Transpar\303\252ncia constante.\" I must also implement the specified spacing: 12px between the title and helper text, and 16px between the helper text, the arrow, and the subtitle, and consider the need to centralize it.\n\n\n**Refining Integration Plan**\n\nI\'m now implementing the code, and ensuring the arrow is integrated correctly. I\'m focusing on the `flex` and `items-center` properties of the new container, and whether they need to be replaced with more general `grid` or `grid-cols` properties. I am specifically considering how these properties interact with centering directives for the merged content, and how that can be achieved through different alignment techniques.\n\n\n\n**Confirming Element Alignment**\n\nI\'m now confirming the intended left alignment of the content from the third column, and whether centering the entire block aligns with user\'s vision. I\'m focusing on the \"Contencioso\" element, and its placement. I\'ve removed the absolute positioned scroll indicator. I\'m using \"Contencioso\" and its helper text as a new focus.\n\n\n"
