    thinking: "**Analyzing Scroll Indicator Position**\n\nI\'ve been examining the code, and I\'m focusing on how the scroll indicator is rendered. Specifically, I\'m looking at its positioning with the `bottom-2` and `left-1/2` attributes, and how `translate-x-1/2` is used for centering. The visibility conditions for different screen sizes are also key.\n\n\n**Restructuring Vertical Elements**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the grid to vertically order the elements as requested. I\'ve realized the user wants the \"scroll to explore\" indicator combined with the \"\303\211tica\" and \"Transpar\303\252ncia constante\" elements. I\'m focusing on integrating the scroll indicator into the third block, rather than making it a separate block. I\'ll need to adjust the grid layout.\n\n\n**Refining Element Placement**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the positioning. My focus is centralizing that set of four elements correctly. The user\'s goal seems to be centralized, so I\'m testing `text-align: center` and `items-center`. I\'ve also reconsidered the column structure, as placing \"\303\211tica\" below the existing columns might be the intended placement, so I\'m testing `grid-cols-2` and adding a full-width row after, to contain the set of 4 elements.\n\n\n**Simplifying Layout Adjustments**\n\nI\'ve determined I can remove the old scroll indicator div entirely. Now, I\'m integrating that section\'s function directly within the third block\'s structure. I\'m focusing on the `items-center` and `text-align: center` properties of the flexbox for central alignment. I\'m modifying `src/components/Hero.tsx` to reflect these changes, removing the original scroll indicator and updating the affected section for proper positioning.\n\n\n**Refining Gap Constraints**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific gap values for visual spacing. I\'m aiming for at least 12px between the \"\303\211tica\" title and the \"Role para explorar\" text, and a minimum of 16px between the text, arrow, and the \"Transpar\303\252ncia constante\" subtitle. I\'ll be using exact gap properties within the `flex-col` structure for precise control. I\'m testing `gap-[12px]` and `gap-[16px]` to achieve the spacing goal. I will need to make changes to `Hero.tsx`.\n\n\n**Confirming Spacing Implementation**\n\nI\'ve verified the `mb-3` for 12px between the title and auxiliary text and `gap-4` for 16px between the text, arrow, and subtitle. My initial concerns about the taller third column in a `grid-cols-3` layout seem unfounded, as grid items will auto-stretch, or simply grow the row height. Now I\'m considering whether \"\303\211tica\" is intended as a badge, with \"Role para explorar\" integrated. I will need to verify this assumption.\n\n\n**Revising Element Positioning**\n\nI\'m now integrating the set of four elements with full width at the bottom, centering them. I\'m removing it from the grid, taking advantage of the `max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6` wrapper in `Hero`. The flex container will handle alignment. The badge placement still requires adjustment. The proposed layout removes the previous `grid-cols-2` grid.\n\n\n**Adjusting Overlapping Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the overlapping elements. The absolute positioning of the scroll indicator places it directly over the \"\303\211tica\" badge. I\'ll need to move the \"\303\211tica\" badge to resolve the overlap. It\'s likely `grid-cols-2` is the correct layout, as `grid-cols-3` causes the absolute positioning to overlap \"\303\211tica\" at the center of the screen.\n\n\n"
