    thinking: "**Revising Logo Component**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on replacing the old logo with the new images. Specifically, I am focused on fixing the `Logo.tsx` component. The user provided several images, and I have just started implementing the use of the first image (`https://storage.googleapis.com/mush-img-store/53f0f582-3525`). I\'m looking into how to best integrate it.\n\n\n**Clarifying Image Intent**\n\nI need to confirm the user\'s intent. The first image seems to be the \"AG\" monogram on a black background, the second on a white/transparent background. The user wants the second image to be unchanged, but specifically said the *first* image isn\'t the primary logo. I\'m trying to determine which is the final primary logo.\n\n\n**Identifying Logo Variants**\n\nI\'ve got a better handle on the logo options now. I\'ve identified two new images: one horizontal logo, the other vertical, each with \"AG Albuquerque Guerra advogados\" text, and two monograms. The user seems to indicate that the first monogram should be replaced, and the second should remain. I\'m focusing on clarifying which logo is the preferred one.\n\n\n**Implementing Logo Replacement**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the new logo images in `Logo.tsx`. The user wants me to use the provided horizontal and vertical images, and leave the monogram image unchanged. I\'m prioritizing the horizontal and vertical logos based on a variant passed as a prop, and have updated the image URLs accordingly. I also noted that I have identified a total of four images, though the monogram images are the ones to be left as-is, to avoid making further changes.\n\n\n**Refining Image Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s provided images, specifically the horizontal and vertical logos. I\'m moving away from SVG recreation and implementing direct image tags in `Logo.tsx`. Initially, I was unsure if I could directly use the provided storage URLs, but I\'ve realized it\'s safer to download the images locally for more reliable referencing. I\'m planning to use `run_command` with `curl` to download them into the `public/` directory before referencing them in the component.\n\n\n**Downloading Logo Images**\n\nI\'ve got the image URLs now, and I\'m ready to download them. I am going to use `wget` to download the horizontal and vertical logos, as well as the monogram, for local use in the `Logo.tsx` component. The horizontal logo will be saved as `public/logo-horizontal.png`, the vertical logo as `public/logo-vertical.png`, and the monogram image as `public/logo-monogram.png`.\n\n\n**Confirming Final Image Use**\n\nI\'m now re-examining `Logo.tsx` based on the user\'s explicit comments. I\'ve noted the user indicated the *second* image, which I understand to be `/logo-monogram.png` is the desired logo. I am confirming my approach to ensure this image is the primary focus, and the horizontal and vertical images are appropriately handled.\n\n```tsx\nimport React from \'react\';\n\ninterface LogoProps {\n  className?: string;\n  variant?: \'horizontal\' | \'vertical\' | \'monogram\';\n}\n\nexport const Logo: React.FC<LogoProps> = ({ className = \'\', variant = \'horizontal\' }) => {\n  if (variant === \'vertical\') {\n    return (\n      <img src=\"/logo-vertical.png\" alt=\"Albuquerque Guerra Advogados\" className={`w-32 md:w-40 object-contain ${className}`} />\n    );\n  }\n  if (variant === \'monogram\') {\n    return (\n      <img src=\"/logo-monogram.png\" alt=\"AG Advogados\" className={`w-12 md:w-16 object-contain ${className}`} />\n    );\n  }\n  return (\n    <img src=\"/logo-horizontal.png\" alt=\"Albuquerque Guerra Advogados\" className={`h-12 md:h-16 object-contain ${className}`} />\n  );\n};\n```\n\n\n**Interpreting User Instructions**\n\nI\'m now carefully interpreting the user\'s instructions regarding the images. It seems the user wants the second image (\"AG\" on a dark background) to be the one that is unchanged. They are requesting that the \"first\" image, which appears to be the Hero section screenshot, be removed from the logo component. I\'m focusing on ensuring these images are correctly implemented.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the correct implementation. The user explicitly wants the *second* image, which I\'ve identified as the monogram, to be left unchanged. The first image is the screenshot. I\'m removing the screenshot from the `Logo.tsx` component. I\'m also confirming that I have identified five images in total, including the horizontal and vertical logos. I\'m focusing on ensuring these images are correctly implemented, with priority given to the monogram.\n\n\n"
